<manifest version="1.0" type="device">
    <hal format="hidl">
        <name>android.hardware.audio</name>
        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
        <version>2.0</version>
        <interface>
            <name>IDevicesFactory</name>
            <instance>default</instance>
        </interface>
    </hal>
    <!-- android.hardware.audio.effect@2.0::IEffectsFactory/default has no
         standalone hwbinder service anywhere in this tree; only the
         passthrough-style android.hardware.audio.effect@2.0-impl.so
         (PRODUCT_PACKAGES in hidl.mk, confirmed built and installed to
         /vendor/lib(64)/hw/ for both architectures), matching upstream
         AOSP's own default implementation, which never ships a separate
         "-service" binary for this HAL either.

         This entry previously declared <transport>hwbinder</transport>,
         which does not match: LegacySupport's registerPassthroughServiceImplementation()
         calls getRawServiceInternal(..., getStub=true), which in turn
         calls IServiceManager::getTransport() and expects the manifest to
         say "passthrough" for anything it's going to dlopen directly
         rather than reach over hwbinder; with "hwbinder" declared here
         instead, that resolution mismatched what's actually provided and
         the passthrough load failed ("Could not get passthrough
         implementation for android.hardware.audio.effect@2.0::IEffectsFactory/default"),
         so AudioFlinger's createEffect() (IAudioFlinger transaction 41)
         had nothing to talk to, hung, and eventually tripped AudioFlinger's
         own TimeCheck watchdog, aborting audioserver and stalling video
         playback (apps sync to the audio clock) every ~15-20s regardless
         of video codec/resolution. Fixed by declaring the transport as
         passthrough, matching how android.hardware.graphics.mapper and
         android.hardware.sensors are declared further down in this same
         file for the same reason (passthrough-only implementations, no
         separate service process).

         Earlier attempt history, kept for reference: removing this <hal>
         entry entirely (to match the DRM HAL fix elsewhere in this file)
         was tried and made things categorically worse; libaudiohal.so's
         EffectsFactoryHalInterface::create() -> createPreferredImpl()
         does not gracefully handle the case where NO version of this HAL
         is declared in the manifest at all; it null-derefs inside
         strlen() and audioserver hard-crashes with SIGSEGV on every
         single boot (a full bootloop), which is strictly worse than the
         previous watchdog-crash. Do not remove this entry again. -->
    <hal format="hidl">
        <name>android.hardware.audio.effect</name>
        <transport arch="32+64">passthrough</transport>
        <version>2.0</version>
        <interface>
            <name>IEffectsFactory</name>
            <instance>default</instance>
        </interface>
    </hal>
    <hal format="hidl">
